      "level": 2,
      "content": "Drainage Patterns of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Indus Waters Treaty (1960) between India and Pakistan allocated the eastern rivers (Ravi, Beas, Sutlej) to India.",
        "The major Himalayan river systems in India include the Indus, Ganga, and Brahmaputra river systems.",
        "Key prominent cities situated along the Ganga river include Haridwar, Kanpur, Prayagraj, Varanasi, Patna, and Kolkata.",
        "Indian drainage is broadly divided into Himalayan versus Peninsular systems, as well as East-flowing versus West-flowing rivers."
      ],
      "id": "40g0qns"
    },
